Water and Wastewater Treatment Engineering — MIT 1.85 (@wu-mit185: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_396YEC55H29CR6J4ZBZX5JBY60
Peter Shanahan. MIT 1.85, Spring 2006, graduate level. [Course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/1-85-water-and-wastewater-treatment-engineering-spring-2006/) · [Lecture notes](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/1-85-water-and-wastewater-treatment-engineering-spring-2006/pages/lecture-notes/).

Work the complete public sequence, problem sets, examinations and design project. Use reactor reasoning and kinetics to connect physical, chemical and biological treatment. Reconstruct the assumptions behind a unit calculation and carry the resulting flow and composition into the next process. Compare the historical course's design choices with later evidence and current requirements.

MIT lists notes, assignments and solutions, examinations and project examples; full lecture video is not promised. OCW's CC BY-NC-SA terms apply with its exclusions and separate third-party notices. Commercial readings cited by the course are not thereby supplied or licensed for copying. The date is part of the citation.

